    {
      "title": "Nearly 200 students injured in French schools protests as clashes with police continue – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/05/europe-spain-pedro-sanchez-election-housing-france-school-protests-ukraine-russia-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Hundreds of schools in France remain closed amid planned demonstrations across the country</p><p><strong>The conservative People’s Party is very pleased with the announcement.</strong></p><p><strong>“At last,”</strong> they say on their X, with a slick election video – set to the EU’s anthem “Ode to Joy” – to go along with it.</p><p><strong>Spanish prime minister Pedro Sánchez has called a snap election for 29 November,</strong> just days after rightwing parties blocked his minority government’s emergency measures on housing amid widespread protests (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/05/europe-spain-pedro-sanchez-election-housing-france-school-protests-ukraine-russia-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ac34d298f085bd691f923b2#block-6ac34d298f085bd691f923b2\">9:10</a>).</p><p><strong>The election will take place on Sunday, 29 November,</strong> the earliest possible date procedurally.</p><p>In a fierce address, <strong>Sánchez framed the election as choice between “regressing” under a “far-right coalition” or “keeping moving forward” with his progressive administration</strong> (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/05/europe-spain-pedro-sanchez-election-housing-france-school-protests-ukraine-russia-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ac34bad8f08733ed3bf1feb#block-6ac34bad8f08733ed3bf1feb\">9:04</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/05/europe-spain-pedro-sanchez-election-housing-france-school-protests-ukraine-russia-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ac34d0a8f085bd691f923b1#block-6ac34d0a8f085bd691f923b1\">9:09</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/05/europe-spain-pedro-sanchez-election-housing-france-school-protests-ukraine-russia-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ac34ec48f08733ed3bf2005#block-6ac34ec48f08733ed3bf2005\">9:17</a>).</p><p>He said <strong>the election will be about who will guide Spain through a period of disruption</strong> amid high political tensions, global instability, climate emergency, and uncertainty posed by the rise of AI (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/05/europe-spain-pedro-sanchez-election-housing-france-school-protests-ukraine-russia-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ac34e058f0864af62913090#block-6ac34e058f0864af62913090\">9:13</a>).</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/05/europe-spain-pedro-sanchez-election-housing-france-school-protests-ukraine-russia-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-05T15:59:30"
    },
    {
      "title": "France braces for national day of school protests as boy loses hand",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/05/schoolboy-loses-hand-police-stun-grenade-french-school-protests",
      "description": "<p>Thousands expected to join marches of support on Tuesday across the country amid growing concerns over police response</p><p>France is bracing for a national day of protests and high-school blockades as a youth protest movement gathers pace amid a growing debate over the scale of the police response.<strong> </strong></p><p>In one incident, a 15-year-old protesting against what demonstrators said were France’s dilapidated ⁠and understaffed ​schools ‌had his hand ‌blown off outside a high school<strong> </strong> in the northern town of Lens, said François-Xavier Lauch, the prefect of Pas-de-Calais.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/05/schoolboy-loses-hand-police-stun-grenade-french-school-protests\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-05T15:50:50"
    }
  ]
